WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.7 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Monitoring: planned versus actual

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Monitoring compares what you planned with what is actually happening, from your first activity.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.541
Monitoring compares what you planned with what is actually happening. For each indicator and period you record the planned value, the actual value and the gap, then ask why.

4
00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:26.541
Record, explain, then act

5
00:00:26.541 --> 00:00:37.500
Record the gap: Planned value, actual value and the difference, for each indicator and period. For example: Planned 20 repair café visitors in May; actual 12; a gap of 8.

6
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:47.348
Ask why first: Check the data, the assumptions, the context and whether the target was realistic. For example: Visits fell because the local market moved to Saturdays.

7
00:00:47.348 --> 00:00:58.396
Show the status: Green on track, amber at risk, red off track, with one line of comment. For example: Amber: sessions move to Saturday mornings from June.

8
00:00:58.796 --> 00:00:59.396
Why it matters

9
00:00:59.396 --> 00:01:05.070
1. Gaps show up early, while they are still cheap to fix.

10
00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:10.004
2. Explaining before reacting stops you fixing the wrong problem.

11
00:01:10.004 --> 00:01:16.678
3. A simple dashboard keeps co-founders and partners on the same page.

12
00:01:17.078 --> 00:01:17.678
What it feeds

13
00:01:17.678 --> 00:01:22.611
1. Your learning reviews: the dashboard is the starting point.

14
00:01:22.611 --> 00:01:27.174
2. Your evaluation: monitoring data is its raw material.

15
00:01:27.174 --> 00:01:33.848
3. Your reports: planned versus actual is what funders often ask for.

16
00:01:34.248 --> 00:01:34.848
What to avoid

17
00:01:34.848 --> 00:01:39.411
Reacting to one number instead of the trend.

18
00:01:39.411 --> 00:01:43.233
Blaming people before checking the data.

19
00:01:43.233 --> 00:01:49.907
A dashboard with too many indicators to read in a minute.

20
00:01:50.507 --> 00:01:52.307
You design your monitoring dashboard and review routine.

21
00:01:52.307 --> 00:01:56.307
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:01:57.807 --> 00:02:00.907
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
